[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2699427137","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103567#issuecomment-2699427137","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103567","id":2699427137,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6g5f1B","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-05T00:54:04Z","updated_at":"2025-03-05T00:55:47Z","body":"I believe this was done by design. We discussed this during the shadowmask implementation and it was best to proceed this way, as it made the implementation simpler. Also, in terms of discoverability, it's best to have a dedicated property to control shadowmask display behavior.\n\nInstead, there should be a dedicated way to set an \"always shadowmask\" mode that samples static object shadows from the shadowmask exclusively (regardless of distance), and only samples the shadowmap for dynamic objects that aren't baked into the shadowmask.\n\nSee comments in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/77284 (especially my [review comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/77284#issuecomm